 HTML: scan on*/javascript:/data: attributes on every start tag
 
 html_attributes() only ran for tags in %elements/%tricks, so script in
 event-handler attributes on anything else was never collected -- e.g. an
 <rect onclick=...> inside an inline <svg> in an attached .htm, a live
 phishing pattern.  Browsers fire on* handlers on any element, so a tag
 whitelist is trivially bypassed.  Call html_attributes() for every start
 tag; rendering, URI and tag-ratio handling still apply only to known
 elements, so HTML stats are unchanged.
 
 Adds t/data/nice/handler_javascript_svg_attach covering an SVG <rect
 onclick> and a custom <foo onmouseover> in an HTML attachment.
 
 
