 Bug 8415: FreeMail: stop clobbering the cached body array
 
 _parse_body() aliased $_ to the elements of the array returned by
 get_decoded_stripped_body_text_array(), which is the message's cached
 rendered body. The s/// calls that blank out addresses we don't want to
 harvest therefore rewrote the body in place, permanently, so every body
 rule evaluated after FreeMail saw a corrupted message: addresses in <>
 were gone, bare addresses followed by a short lowercase word and a colon
 took that trailing word with them, and any URL containing @ or %40 was
 stripped. Forwarded mail was affected the most.
 
 Copy each line into a lexical before stripping so the harvesting logic is
 unchanged but the cached body is left alone.
 
 
