 Handler::Image: prefer heif-dec, document optional external programs
 
 Bug 8421: the handler framework's optional external dependencies were
 undiscoverable.  tesseract and libheif were not checked for or mentioned 
by
 Makefile.PL, absent from INSTALL, and only tesseract was named in 
UPGRADE --
 so users had no warning before upgrading that both pull in substantial
 recursive dependencies.  The reporter also hit heif-convert being 
missing on
 FreeBSD, where the packager drops the compatibility symlink libheif adds 
for
 the tool's pre-1.18 name.
 
 Use heif-dec, the canonical name since libheif 1.18, falling back to
 heif-convert so installs carrying only the older name keep working.
 _resolve_binary() now takes a list of candidate names for this.
 
 Rename the config setting image_heif_convert_path to image_heif_dec_path 
to
 match.  No compatibility alias: the Image handler is new in 4.0.3, which 
is
 still unreleased, so the old name has never shipped and cannot appear in 
any
 existing user config.
 
 Document the optional external programs in a new INSTALL section (gpg,
 curl/wget/fetch, re2c, tesseract, heif-dec, pdftotext, unrar), expand
 UPGRADE's Image entry to cover libheif and say why the handler is not 
enabled
 by default, and note the dependency in v403.pre.
 
 Add tesseract, heif-dec, pdftotext and unrar to DependencyInfo's optional
 binaries so Makefile.PL reports them, each noting which handler needs it 
and
 that the handler is not loaded by default.
 
 The Image handler is already disabled by default in v403.pre, and the 
tests
 already skip cleanly when the binaries are absent; both were verified.
 
 
